'''KSL-FM''' (102.7 FM) is a [[commercial radio]] station [[Community of license|licensed]] to [[Midvale, Utah]], and serving the [[Salt Lake City metropolitan area]]. KSL-FM and [[sister station]] [[KSL (AM)|KSL]] (1160 AM) [[simulcast]] a [[talk radio|news-talk]] [[radio format]]. They are owned by [[Bonneville International]], a wholly-owned broadcasting subsidiary of [[the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints]] (LDS). The two stations, alongside co-owned television station [[KSL-TV]], maintain studio facilities in the Broadcast House building at the [[Triad Center]] in downtown [[Salt Lake City]].

KSL-FM is a [[list of broadcast station classes#FM|Class C]] station.  It has an [[effective radiated power]] (ERP) of 25,000 watts.<REF>[https://radio-locator.com/info/KSL-FM Radio-Locator.com/KSL-FM]</REF>  The KSL-FM [[transmitter]] site is on [[Farnsworth Peak]], part of the [[Oquirrh Mountains]] in [[Erda, Utah|Erda]], southwest of Salt Lake City.  It is co-located with the KSL-TV [[radio masts and towers|tower]].  KSL-FM broadcasts using [[HD Radio]] technology.  Its HD2 [[digital subchannel|subchannel]] rebroadcasts the [[sports radio]] format on 1280 [[KZNS (AM)|KZNS]].  The HD3 subchannel carries the [[Latter-day Saints Channel]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.hdradio.com/stations|title = HD Radio Stations}}</ref>
